/* ============================== ROOT ============================== */
/* ============================== CARD BUREAU · POPULATION · ORG ==============================
   Three things live here.

   1. Card Bureau — issuing and re-issuing the Marbella ID card. A card opens doors that are
      shut to outsiders, so a replacement is not a printing job, it is a small investigation.
      Two paths, deliberately unequal:
        · Damaged / worn card handed back  → three ticks and an authorisation. Seconds.
        · Lost, stolen or unreturned       → reason, circumstances, undertakings, authorisation.
      Either way the old card is killed and every issue is written to a log that is only ever
      appended to.

   2. Population — who we have, where they sit, which office they report to.

   3. Org — who reports to whom, drawn as a tree that grows as HR enters people.

   HONEST NOTE ON THE AUTHORISATION CODE: everything here runs in the browser, so the code is
   checked in the browser. That is fine for stopping a colleague printing a card off someone
   else's screen. It is NOT access control — anyone who can open the file can read the code.
   Real enforcement belongs on the server that talks to the printer, and that is a backend job.  */

